WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:07.459
Fear, alienation, and loneliness: these are
the emotions that Rahmat associates with Kabul.

00:00:07.459 --> 00:00:12.940
Last December, the 23 year-old returned here
on the first deportation flight from Germany,

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:15.530
where he'd lived for six years.

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:20.519
He's afraid to show his face, for fear of
the Taliban, from whom he had fled at the

00:00:20.519 --> 00:00:23.060
time.

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:32.150
"The Taliban murdered my father, because he
was a famous general - that's why I fled.

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:37.770
If they find me, they'll kill me too.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:39.900
I'm afraid.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:41.640
It's not safe here."

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.680
Rahmat looks at pictures from Germany.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:49.809
He misses his friends from the vocational
school he attended until 2012, when his asylum

00:00:49.809 --> 00:00:51.949
application was rejected.

00:00:51.949 --> 00:00:57.809
Migration officials didn't believe his story,
and four years later they deported him.

00:00:57.809 --> 00:01:04.610
"It's not fair - after six years there, we
were integrating.

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:07.930
I learned the language, I did training.

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:12.650
It was never easy, but we did it, and I think
it's wrong that they would simply kick us

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:15.220
out."

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:18.290
Today he has an appointment at the aid organization
AMAZO.

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:23.990
Its founder, Abdul Ghaffoor willingly went
back to Afghanistan a few years ago.

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:29.530
Now he's helping deportees like Rahmat, providing
counseling and emotional support, and helping

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:31.330
them find work.

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:36.180
"They are in a situation that they do not
know where to go.

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:37.860
They don’t have families.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:40.070
They do not have a network here.

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:42.420
They don’t know how to find work.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:47.530
They're afraid of the security situation - So
yes you're sending people back to nothing

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:51.450
- as a result, what happens is that because
they don’t have anything here.

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:54.430
They don’t find hope; they don’t find
any mean of survival.

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:58.770
What happens - as soon as they are deported
back, they leave the country again."

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:02.270
Rahmat is staying with friends.

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:05.680
But it's hard for him; he doesn't want to
burden them.

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:08.750
And he doesn't dare to return to his home
in Ghasni.

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:11.390
He doesn't know where his mother and brother
are living.

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:15.040
Like many refugees, he's lost contact.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:20.230
"I've tried to locate my mother, but I just
don't know where she is.

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:25.860
I don't even know if she's alive or dead."

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:29.040
Fleeing to Europe again isn't an option for
Rahmat.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:31.700
He doesn't have the money to pay the smugglers.

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:33.850
And he has no prospects either.

00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:40.330
For now, he exists in a vacuum, neither welcome
in Germany nor Afghanistan, living somewhere

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:42.300
between the past and the present.

